## Interpretation

- **ABR on vs off delta:** ABR reduces downshifts under congestion by tracking network capacity; off shows static bitrate behavior.
- **Shape × encoder:** compare cells only within one encoder class — an integrated VA part can have a ~45fps ceiling (p50 encode ~19ms) where a discrete NVENC card holds 60fps (p50 ~2ms). Per-host hardware facts: `_shared/hosts.json` notes.
- **present_sd p95 ≥ 18ms** → hitch threshold crossed (`hitchSdThresholdMs=18.0`).
- **encode_ms p95 ≥ 16ms** → encoder saturation signal (`encoderCeilingMs=16.0`).

